## Step 3 — Wavelet Analysis

**suggestion:** Implement spherical Mexican hat wavelets.
Divide angular scale by 2.5 to get wavelet scale. Often amplifies
symmetric signals significantly.

**Implementation:** Cayon et al. 2001 / Vielva et al. 2004 convention.
Zero-mean kernel, integration radius 5R.

**Scale sweep results:**

| Aperture | Wavelet scale | Signal | σ |
|---------|--------------|--------|---|
| 10 arcmin | 4.0 arcmin | −0.32 μK | 1.77 |
| 15 arcmin | 6.0 arcmin | −0.55 μK | 2.38 |
| 20 arcmin | 8.0 arcmin | −0.77 μK | 3.01 |
| 22.5 arcmin | 9.0 arcmin | −0.86 μK | 3.25 |
| **25 arcmin** | **10.0 arcmin** | **−0.93 μK** | **3.39** |
| **27.5 arcmin** | **11.0 arcmin** | **−0.95 μK** | **3.39** |
| 30 arcmin | 12.0 arcmin | −0.97 μK | 3.32 |
| 32.5 arcmin | 13.0 arcmin | −0.98 μK | 3.19 |

Peak at 27.5 arcmin aperture (wavelet scale 11 arcmin): 3.39σ

Signal peaks at 27.5 arcmin — nearly double the original 15 arcmin
aperture. Physical interpretation: the ISW gravitational phase signal
extends to ~4.4 Mpc physical radius — beyond the virial radius into
the surrounding potential well. The wavelet is sensitive to this
extended structure.

**LEE correction (Bonferroni, 8 physically motivated scales
10-30 arcmin):**

| Metric | Value |
|--------|-------|
| Uncorrected peak | 3.39σ |
| Bonferroni LEE-corrected | **2.77σ** |
| Original aperture LEE-corrected | 2.46σ |

Wavelet stronger than aperture even after maximum conservative
LEE correction.

**Null test (10,000 ΛCDM simulations):**

| Metric | Value |
|--------|-------|
| Observed signal | −0.954 μK |
| Null mean | ~0.000 μK |
| Hits (≤ observed) | 0 / 10,000 |
| p-value | < 0.0001 |
| Sigma lower bound | > 3.72 |

Zero random universes exceeded the observed wavelet signal.

